        "id": "navigation",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "**Executive dashboard · Page 3 of 3**  \n[1. Marketplace Overview](page_1_marketplace_overview.html) · [2. Marketplace Efficiency](page_2_marketplace_efficiency.html) · **3. Growth Quality & Operating Priorities**"
      },
      {
        "id": "priority_summary",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Operating priorities\n\nManhattan and Brooklyn added **318,282 completed trips**, equivalent to **100.7%** of net city growth because declines elsewhere offset part of their increase. The wait decomposition assigns **0.449 minutes** of the citywide change to within-borough movement, while geographic mix contributed **-0.008 minutes** and slightly offset the deterioration.\n\nThe hourly view identifies **03:00** as the largest year-over-year wait increase at **18.5%**. The recurring-window ranking is dominated by JFK and LaGuardia late-evening and overnight periods, while the neighborhood list concentrates on Harlem, Brownsville, Crown Heights, Canarsie, Stuyvesant Heights, Bushwick, Mott Haven, and East New York.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "priority_metrics",
        "type": "metric-strip",
        "cardIds": [
          "core_growth_card",
          "within_borough_card",
          "peak_hour_card",
          "top_window_card"
        ]
      },
