        "layout": "full"
      },
      {
        "id": "recommended_actions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Recommended actions\n\n1. **Protect airport service quality.** Review late-evening and overnight operating playbooks at JFK and LaGuardia, beginning with the highest-burden weekday-hour windows in the table.\n2. **Target neighborhood diagnostics before broad demand stimulation.** Prioritize localized dispatch, driver-positioning, and pickup-process tests in the ranked Harlem, Brooklyn, and Bronx zones; measure completed trips and Request-to-Pickup together.\n3. **Treat 00:00–07:00 as a focused service-recovery window.** Diagnose the 03:00–06:00 wait increase and evaluate targeted interventions with citywide and zone-level guardrails.\n4. **Add the missing causal evidence before making supply claims.** Join cancellations, driver online time, dispatch acceptance, surge, promotions, and pickup-process data before attributing the observed patterns to supply shortage or estimating financial impact.\n"
      }
